        "title": "Arrays und Schleifen",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148278,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Lass uns lernen, wie man Funktionen verwendet, um Arrays zu durchlaufen und ihre Werte zu manipulieren, wann immer wir wollen, zum Beispiel wenn wir in einem Spiel eine Taste drücken.</p><p>Führe den untenstehenden Code aus, der überprüft, ob der Wert <code>3</code> im <code>enemyLevels</code>-Array mithilfe einer Funktion existiert.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (enemyLevels[i] === search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enemy level found!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, search);\" /></content></code></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148279,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Funktionen sind nützlich, wenn wir wiederverwendbaren Code ausführen möchten.</p><p>Um auf Array-Elemente mit der <code>searchEnemyLevel</code>-Funktion zuzugreifen, lass uns das <code>enemyLevels</code>-Array übergeben, wenn wir die Funktion aufrufen.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"122\" endIndex=\"133\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>enemyLevels</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148280,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wenn wir auf Elemente zugreifen möchten, die in mehreren Arrays gespeichert sind, übergeben wir die Arrays als Argumente, wenn wir die Funktion aufrufen.</p><p>Lass uns das zweite Array <code>enemyLevels2</code> codieren, wenn wir <code>searchEnemyLevel()</code> aufrufen.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\":\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"210\" endIndex=\"211\" /><option startIndex=\"212\" endIndex=\"224\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels2 = [\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, enemyLevels2\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels2);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, enemyLevels2);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>,</code>, gefolgt von <code>enemyLevels2</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148281,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Sobald wir ein Array an eine Funktion übergeben haben, können wir über die Array-Elemente iterieren. Erstelle eine <code>for</code>-Schleife, um durch alle Elemente zu iterieren.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" len = enemyLevels.length;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; len; i++) {}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"while\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"{\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"}\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"110\" endIndex=\"113\" /><option startIndex=\"114\" endIndex=\"115\" /><option startIndex=\"138\" endIndex=\"139\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>for</code>, gefolgt von <code>(</code> und schließlich <code>)</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148282,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Um jedes Array-Element innerhalb einer <code>for</code>-Schleife abzurufen, verwenden wir die Syntax <code>array[i]</code>, wobei <code>i</code> die aktuelle Iteration ist und <code>array</code> der Array-Name ist.</p><p>Lass uns den Code schreiben, um einzelne <code>enemyLevels</code>-Elemente abzurufen.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"138\" endIndex=\"152\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>enemyLevels[i]</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148283,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Indem wir eine Funktion, ein Array und einen weiteren Parameter verwenden, können wir viel erreichen.</p><p>Zum Beispiel, lass uns nach dem Element <code>3</code> im <code>enemyLevels</code>-Array suchen, indem wir <code>enemyLevels</code> und dann <code>search</code> an die <code>searchEnemyLevel</code>-Funktion übergeben.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"262\" endIndex=\"273\" /><option startIndex=\"273\" endIndex=\"274\" /><option startIndex=\"275\" endIndex=\"281\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (enemyLevels[i] === search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enemy level found!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, search);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>enemyLevels</code>, gefolgt von <code>,</code> und schließlich <code>search</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148284,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wir können auch mehrere Arrays mit einer Funktion verwenden, um eine bestimmte Aktion auszuführen, wie zum Beispiel gemeinsame Array-Elemente zu finden.</p><p>Lass uns gemeinsame Elemente in zwei Arrays finden, indem wir sie an die <code>compareArrays</code>-Funktion übergeben.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"263\" endIndex=\"271\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" one = [\" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" two = [\" /><text value=\"90\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"55\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"compareArrays\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"one, two\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; one.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (one[i] === two[i]) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Same value at this index:&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", one[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"compareArrays(one, two);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>one, two</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148285,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wie greifen wir innerhalb einer Funktion auf Array-Elemente zu?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Wir übergeben das Array an die Funktion</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Wir rufen das Array direkt auf, ohne es an die Funktion zu übergeben</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wir übergeben das Array an die Funktion.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148286,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Was zeigt dieser Code in der Konsole an?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerScores = [\" /><text value=\"2500\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"displayPlayers\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"playerNames, playerScores\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerNames);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerScores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"displayPlayers(playerNames, playerScores);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Es zeigt mehrere Arrays an</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Es zeigt nur das erste Array an</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Es zeigt mehrere Arrays an.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148287,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Was können wir innerhalb einer Funktion verwenden, um über ein an die Funktion übergebenes Array zu iterieren?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Wir können eine <code>for</code>-Schleife verwenden </item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Wir können eine <code>if</code>-Anweisung verwenden</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wir können eine <code>for</code>-Schleife verwenden .</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148288,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Was passiert, wenn wir <code>playerNames[i]</code> innerhalb einer <code>for</code>-Schleife wie in der Funktion unten verwenden?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchPlayer\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"playerNames\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; playerNames.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerNames[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchPlayer(playerNames);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Wir rufen die Array-Elemente nacheinander ab</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Wir rufen Array-Elemente alle auf einmal ab</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wir rufen die Array-Elemente nacheinander ab.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148289,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Was zeigt dieser Code in der Konsole an?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" items = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Key&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Gem&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchItem\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"items, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; items.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (items[i] == search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;The item exists!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchItem(items, search);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Es zeigt nichts an</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Es zeigt <code>The item exists!</code> an</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Es zeigt nichts an.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 148290,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Warum übergeben wir mehrere Arrays an eine Funktion?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Um eine bestimmte Aktion auszuführen, die Informationen aus mehreren Arrays enthält</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Um eine bestimmte Aktion auszuführen, die Informationen aus nur einem Array enthält</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Um eine bestimmte Aktion auszuführen, die Informationen aus mehreren Arrays enthält.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 148291,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Beim Aufruf der <code>displayScores</code>-Funktion, programmiere den Wert, um das <code>scores</code>-Array anzuzeigen.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"106\" endIndex=\"114\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"1200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2400\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3600\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"displayScores\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(scores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"displayScores(scores);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>(scores)</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #15",
            "id": 148292,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Zeige die <code>scores</code>- und <code>bonuses</code>-Arrays an, indem du sie an die <code>searchBonus</code>-Funktion übergibst.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"167\" endIndex=\"173\" /><option startIndex=\"173\" endIndex=\"174\" /><option startIndex=\"175\" endIndex=\"182\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"1200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2400\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3600\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" bonuses = [\" /><text value=\"50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"150\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchBonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores, bonuses\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(scores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(bonuses);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchBonus(scores, bonuses);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>scores</code>, gefolgt von <code>,</code> und schließlich <code>bonuses</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #16",
            "id": 148293,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Lass den Code über alle <code>scores</code>-Elemente iterieren.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"while\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"[\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"]\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"104\" endIndex=\"105\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"1200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2400\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3600\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"getScores\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; scores.length; i++) {}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"getScores(scores);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>for</code>, gefolgt von <code>(</code> und schließlich <code>)</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
